    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_e4e73b10",
        "filename": "keystone/token/providers/common.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 284,
      "author": {
        "id": 7191
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-13T22:15:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right - ayoung and i had a debate over this as to whether it was necessary to put true - because True is the default, it\u0027s False we\u0027re really interested in here.\n\nWhat i most dislike is you are looking for the admin role rather than just saying everything is in the admin project. I don\u0027t want to make the string \u0027admin\u0027 any more special than it already is.\n\nBut yea - if nothing is in the token then we assume True. Adding True here doesn\u0027t buy us anything.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_9995ffe5",
      "revId": "c2faedc19e63122a3a7d846abb04a96d5c7de060",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_87358847",
        "filename": "keystone/token/providers/common.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 284,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-14T13:45:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "checking for the admin role is essential. Otherwise as soon as the code and policy files for nova, etc. are updated to check for is_admin_project\u003dTrue and consider that global, ALL role assignments will be global for environments that don\u0027t have the admin project specified in keystone\u0027s conf. Doing that for admin is backward compatible because that\u0027s the current behavior for admin roles... but doing that for anything else is most definitely NOT backward compatible.\n\nAnd the fact that keystoneauth will assume True if is_admin_project isn\u0027t in the token only helps those that use keystoneauth... which is not everyone. So doing this here rather than just in keystoneauth means it works for everyone, not just users of keystoneauth.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_e4e73b10",
      "revId": "c2faedc19e63122a3a7d846abb04a96d5c7de060",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_47643221",
        "filename": "keystone/token/providers/common.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 284,
      "author": {
        "id": 7191
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-15T23:02:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All roles aren\u0027t magically going to become global - that would require rewriting the policy files. admin is by convention the only role that is used across projects but all roles work the same way here. \n\nkeystoneauth is required to expose the flag via auth_token middleware. auth_token middleware and oslo.context are what is required to do enforcement properly.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_87358847",
      "revId": "c2faedc19e63122a3a7d846abb04a96d5c7de060",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dab17558_0cccebb9",
        "filename": "keystone/token/providers/common.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 284,
      "author": {
        "id": 10608
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-05-16T14:52:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that rewriting of policy files is exactly what is going to start happening, though, making all roles global-capable. That is only safe, for the reasons I described above, if we check for the admin role here.",
      "parentUuid": "dab17558_47643221",
      "revId": "c2faedc19e63122a3a7d846abb04a96d5c7de060",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
